# O10-PERF acceptance (tests/probes/listening-o10p-acceptance.py), written by the independent acceptance author.
# This is the TARGET: every check passes. On main e45d947 through the dev script it fails S1-S4 (no GStreamer in the dev shell)
# and so every media oracle (nothing plays; X1/X2 need GStreamer too); with GStreamer supplied from outside (diagnostic)
# C2, C2w, C3, C3b, C5, G7, M2, M3, M4, U2, U3, U4 fail for their own reasons. Evidence and readings: the O10p acceptance report.
# Entries with @@ declare the measured part of the name; everything else must match exactly.
S1 the dev shell provides GStreamer playbin3 to the window (the probe adds none)
S2 the elements the catalogue loops need are in the dev shell (qtdemux, h264parse, avdec_h264, videoconvert, playbin3)
S3 the dev shell decodes a catalogue loop end to end (all frames of room-night-drive.mp4)
S4 the dev shell GStreamer is pinned to exactly the package's plugin packages (same store paths)
S5 the 8 catalogue room loops are unchanged in format (h264 1440x810, 480 frames): cost is not cut by shrinking the media
C0 every cold start reached the Rooms grid with its cards (3 runs)
C1 time to Rooms after a cold start is measured and reported (median @@ ms wall, @@ ms GTK-thread CPU, load @@)
C2 the GTK thread is never held more than 50 ms by art during cold start, by GTK-thread CPU (worst @@ ms)
C2w ... and by wall time: <= 50 ms, scaled by the 1-minute load above 8 (worst @@ ms against @@ ms)
C3 poster decoding leaves the GTK thread: no image decode or scale call ran on it during cold start
C3b the GTK thread spent at most 50 ms CPU on art in total during cold start (worst @@ ms)
C4 every card ends up showing its own poster art (placeholders, then textures)
C5 card posters are pre-scaled: each card texture is at most 2x its on-screen size
G0 fixture: the Rooms grid shows the catalogue rooms with scene loops (8)
G1 a preview's scene loop plays: its pixels move on screen
G2 the preview sent no controller command, started nothing and no process
G3 the preview is silent: GStreamer worked (elements created) but no audio sink was created
G4 Enter room sends exactly one enter and opens Now
G5 the entered room's loop plays (pixels move)
G6 the loop plays at its native resolution (1440x810): not a downscaled stand-in
G7 scenes still loop: the entered scene keeps moving after its 20 s clip has ended
G8 an off-screen scene stops decoding: media threads use <= 50 ms CPU in 5 s on the Rooms page (@@ ms)
G9 back on Now, the scene moves again
G10 a hidden window stops decoding: media threads use <= 50 ms CPU in 5 s (@@ ms)
G11 shown again, the scene moves again
G12 reduced motion, entered: the scene stays still
G13 reduced motion shows the still texture at full resolution (not a card-size thumbnail)
G14 reduced motion decodes nothing: media threads <= 50 ms CPU in 4 s (@@ ms)
G15 reduced motion, preview: the scene stays still and the preview stays inert
G16 motion back on: the entered room's scene moves again
scene: the child finished without a crash or hang
scene: the child reported all its oracles and exited 0
M0 fixture: 8 catalogue loop rooms (8 distinct loop files) and 16 user-clip rooms
M1 every catalogue loop visibly played in its preview before its cost was measured
# KNOWN FAILURE allowed: "M2 [ORIGINAL, superseded by M2r]" is the brief's 400 MB target, kept verbatim and still evaluated;
# the coordinator re-based it in phase 2 (M2r: <= 520 MB total and <= 50 MB per loop after the first). Backlog: further cuts.
!M2 [ORIGINAL, superseded by M2r] steady-state media cost with all 8 catalogue loops shown is under 400 MB (process tree RSS, @@ MB)
M2r media cost with all 8 catalogue loops shown is <= 520 MB and each loop after the first adds <= 50 MB (process tree RSS, @@ MB total, @@ MB per loop)
M3 decoder threads are bounded: at most 16 in the whole process tree, warm and at peak (@@)
M4 the media adds at most 64 threads once every loop was shown (@@)
M5 off-screen loops are paused: media threads use <= 50 ms CPU in 5 s on the grid (@@ ms)
M6 steady state: loops still play in the sampled previews (every 5th of 40)
M7 steady state: over the last 20 previews RSS grows <= 64 MB, threads <= 6, fds <= 12; since warm-up at most twice that
M8 no-teardown guarantee: no GL display or context is left behind per preview (GL threads <= warm)
M9 no-teardown guarantee: no new GStreamer pipeline is built once every loop has been shown (@@ built)
# KNOWN FAILURES allowed: "U1/U2 [ORIGINAL, superseded by U1r/U2r]", kept and still evaluated. Phase 2 judged "bounded"
# against the implementer's LOOP_LIMIT (12 loop files; later clips show their still, since evicting a pipeline would be
# a teardown) and re-based U2 with the coordinator's M2r. U1r/U2r state the revised criteria; reasons in the probe.
!U1 [ORIGINAL, superseded by U1r] every user clip visibly played in its preview
U1r user clips: at least 3 beyond the catalogue get a moving loop (@@ did), clips past the window's loop capacity show their still, and the catalogue loops still play afterwards
!U2 [ORIGINAL, superseded by U2r] user clips are bounded: total media cost with 8 catalogue loops and 16 user clips <= 464 MB (@@ MB)
U2r user clips are bounded: total media cost with 8 catalogue loops and 16 user clips <= 520 MB + 50 MB per user clip with a loop (@@ MB against @@ MB)
U3 user clips are bounded: each of the last 8 clips adds <= 4 MB, <= 1 thread, <= 2 fds (@@)
U4 decoder threads stay bounded with user clips (<= 16, @@)
media: the child finished without a crash or hang
media: the child reported all its oracles and exited 0
X1 stress: at least 200 scene-media stress cycles ran (@@ attempted)
X2 stress: zero crashes over those cycles (@@ crashed children)
X3 stress: every stress child finished all its cycles without raising
